{%- comment -%}
  Language switch.

  The shopper chooses, not the shop. In this market a household reads French
  and Arabic in different proportions per person, and the merchant cannot know
  which of the two the visitor in front of them prefers — so the storefront
  offers both and remembers the answer.

  It lives on the storefront's entry points — the header — and nowhere else.
  A shopper deep in a product page has already chosen how they read; putting
  the control there again spends space on the one screen where every pixel is
  doing conversion work, and a language switch beside an order button is a
  distraction from the order button.

  What it switches is DIRECTION and TYPEFACE, which is everything the theme
  itself controls. It does not translate the merchant's own copy: that copy
  lives in the template, and only the merchant can write it in a second
  language. A switch that flipped the layout and left French text behind
  would be worse than none, so a shop that has not provided Arabic copy can
  turn this off — and it is off until they do.

  The choice is stored in localStorage and applied before first paint by the
  inline script in the layout head, so a returning Arabic reader never sees a
  frame of the French layout first.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.lang_switch_enabled -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign default_dir = settings.text_direction | default: 'ltr'
    assign label_a = settings.lang_a_label | default: 'FR'
    assign label_b = settings.lang_b_label | default: 'ع'
  -%}

  <div class="langsw langsw--{{ size | default: 'sm' }}" data-lang-switch
       data-default-dir="{{ default_dir }}">
    <button class="langsw__opt" type="button" data-lang="ltr"
            aria-pressed="{% if default_dir == 'ltr' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
            lang="fr">{{ label_a }}</button>
    <button class="langsw__opt" type="button" data-lang="rtl"
            aria-pressed="{% if default_dir == 'rtl' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
            lang="ar">{{ label_b }}</button>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
